{"_v":1,"id":"the-woman-in-white-2005","cat":"broadway","bd":{"positive":0,"mixed":0,"negative":3},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":44,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2005/11/18/theater/reviews/the-woman-in-white-a-musical-shrouded-in-gloom.html","d":"2005-11-18","q":"This expensive import from London, based on Wilkie Collins's 1860 novel, is a musical that seems to have been conceived in a perpetual fog bank. Even when the stage is brightly lighted, you feel as if you're peering through thick gauze at characters who never quite come into focus."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":44,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2005/legit/reviews/the-woman-in-white-1200527396/","d":"2005-11-18","q":"But in this solemn, lumbering show, they keep moving while getting nowhere."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":52,"b":"Negative","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/WomanInWhite.html","d":"2005-11-27","q":"Practically everyone else, unfortunately including the ever-reliable Walter Charles as Laura and Marian's crotchety uncle, tends to fade into the background."}],"au":{"score":56,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":56,"c":14,"sr":2.8}}},"tn":[{"yr":60,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":"Andrew Lloyd Webber"},{"yr":60,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":"David Zippel"},{"yr":60,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":null}],"cn":{"t":"Lloyd Webber's foggy Victorian melodrama fails to come into focus, with critics finding the expensive London import feels like a dated throwback hampered by unclear storytelling and characters that never fully materialize.","rc":3},"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":10445368,"p":129,"a":152490}},"ta":"210 W 46th St, New York, NY 10036","vs":{"sl":4,"so":4,"co":5,"am":1,"fa":4},"pd":"2005-10-28","ca":[{"n":"Michael Ball","r":"Count Fosco"},{"n":"Ron Bohmer","r":"Sir Percival Glyde"},{"n":"Adam Brazier","r":"Walter Hartright"},{"n":"Walter Charles","r":"Mr. Fairlie"},{"n":"Angela Christian","r":"Anne Catherick"},{"n":"Maria Friedman","r":"Marian Halcombe"},{"n":"Jill Paice","r":"Laura Fairlie"},{"n":"Richard Todd Adams","r":"Con Man"},{"n":"Justis Bolding","r":"Corn Dolly Girl"},{"n":"Lisa Brescia","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"John Dewar","r":"Mr. Fairlie's Servant"},{"n":"Courtney Glass","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Patty Goble","r":"Nurse"},{"n":"Norman Large","r":"Signal Man"},{"n":"Michael Shawn Lewis","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Elizabeth Loyacano","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Daniel Marcus","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Greg Mills","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Elena Shaddow","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Daniel Torres","r":"Ensemble"}]}